. Sherman’s division on the extreme right"}]]}],["$","div","Army of the Ohio; center-Don Carlos Buell",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Army of the Ohio; center"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Don Carlos Buell"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Advanced over rain-soaked ground while building roads and bridges"}]]}],["$","div","Army of the Mississippi; left wing-John Pope",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Army of the Mississippi; left wing"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"John Pope"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Joined Halleck after the capture of New Madrid and Island No. 10"}]]}]]]}],["$","section","Confederacy",{"className":"command-column #9a3d32","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Confederacy"}],[["$","div","Overall command at Corinth-P.G.T. Beauregard",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Overall command at Corinth"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"P.G.T. Beauregard"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Defended the railroad junction, planned the withdrawal, and evacuated toward Tupelo"}]]}],["$","div","Army of the Mississippi-Braxton Bragg",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Army of the Mississippi"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Braxton Bragg"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Led the principal Confederate army at Corinth and replaced Beauregard in June"}]]}],["$","div","Army of the West-Earl Van Dorn",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Army of the West"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Earl Van Dorn"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Reinforced Beauregard from the Trans-Mississippi and held part of the Corinth defenses"}]]}],["$","div","Corps under Beauregard and Bragg-Leonidas Polk / William J. Hardee",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Corps under Beauregard and Bragg"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Leonidas Polk / William J. Ha